# Test: a capability that cannot be determined warns and ze still starts
# Spec: plan/immediate/spec-kernel-capability-gate.md AC-6
# VALIDATES: a probe that could not reach its evidence produces
# doctor-ipsec-xfrm-unknown at WARNING severity, ze doctor still exits 0, and the
# daemon starts. The message carries the reason the probe gave.
# PREVENTS: a working deployment turned into a dead one by an unreadable probe
# (R-1). The gate runs on every ze start on Linux, so refusing on a question ze
# could not ask is the failure with the widest blast radius in this spec. A
# permission denial is the common cause and no kernel rebuild fixes it.
#
# The probe is forced to the cannot-determine answer, which is the one state a
# healthy host never produces by itself. Without the override this branch would
# be unreachable from the user entry point.
option=env:var=ze.test.kernelcap.xfrm:value=unknown
option=env:var=ze.gnmi.enabled:value=1
option=env:var=ze.gnmi.listen:value=127.0.0.1:19352

tmpfs=ipsec-unknown.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF
vpn {
    ipsec {
        interface lo
        ike-group IKE-1 {
            proposal 1 {
                encryption aes256gcm
                hash sha256
                dh-group 14
            }
        }
        esp-group ESP-1 {
            proposal 1 {
                encryption aes256gcm
            }
        }
        site-to-site {
            peer branch {
                connection-type respond
                remote-address 203.0.113.7
                ike-group IKE-1
                esp-group ESP-1
                authentication {
                    mode pre-shared-secret
                    pre-shared-secret correct-horse-battery-staple
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze doctor --json ipsec-unknown.conf
# Exit 0: a warning does not make the host unready, and it must not.
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=doctor-ipsec-xfrm-unknown
expect=stdout:contains=ze.test.kernelcap.xfrm
reject=stdout:pattern=doctor-ipsec-xfrm-unavailable

cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze config validate ipsec-unknown.conf
expect=exit:code=0
reject=stdout:pattern=config-kernel-capability

cmd=foreground:seq=3:exec=ze explain doctor-ipsec-xfrm-unknown
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=does not refuse a start
